{
  "_comment": [
    "The subject catalogue, so contributors pick a subject instead of typing one.",
    "",
    "Keys are collection keys — <programme>/year-N/<branch>, or .../common where",
    "that year is not split. Values are the subjects taught there. `name` is",
    "required; `code` is strongly encouraged, because the code is what groups a",
    "subject's papers together on the site.",
    "",
    "## Why this is empty",
    "",
    "These lists have to come from the actual MUJ curriculum. Inventing subject",
    "codes would be worse than having none: a wrong code silently files a paper",
    "under a subject that does not exist, and nobody notices until someone goes",
    "looking for it.",
    "",
    "## It fills itself in as the archive grows",
    "",
    "The picker offers the union of this file and every subject already present",
    "in that collection, so a subject only has to be typed once ever. Adding it",
    "here just means the first contributor does not have to type it."
  ],
